After the short morning meeting, I sit at my desk.
My boss, Thomas, comes over to me.
He is the project manager for the new project.
He puts a piece of paper with some notes on my table.
"Here are some more details for your part, Maya," he says calmly.
He explains exactly what he needs.
He has been a project manager here for ten years.
"I have led many large teams," Thomas says.
"And we have worked on this idea for two months."
I can easily tell.
He is very professional and explains everything clearly.
I look at the new technical plan.
I fortunately understand the system really well.
But there are still many new things in the project.
"Do you have any questions right now?" he asks.
"Not yet," I answer with a smile.
"I will just read everything through first."
"That sounds like a good plan," he says and moves on to the next desk.
I turn on my computer and am ready to begin.
